# UI rules

Build UI with shadcn/ui. Read `components.json` and keep its preset (`style`: `base-nova`, `baseColor`: `taupe`, `iconLibrary`: `lucide`, `rsc`: true). Import UI from `@/components/ui`.

## Before adding a component

1. Reuse `@/components/ui/*` (button, input, card, label, and the rest already in the repo).
2. If it is missing, use the shadcn MCP to see what exists and pull the latest. Install with the `components.json` preset (`npx shadcn@latest add <component>`), which matches [ui.shadcn.com](https://ui.shadcn.com) structure, composition, and naming.
3. Do not invent button, input, dialog, select, table, or form primitives when shadcn/ui already provides them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom button primitive
export function Button({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <button className="bg-black px-4 py-2 text-white">{children}</button>
}

// ✅ GOOD — shadcn button and its variants
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"

<Button variant="default" size="lg">Save</Button>
```

## Styling and forms

- Style with Tailwind. Extend a shadcn `variant` or `size` instead of restyling the primitive with one-off classes.
- Forms use shadcn form patterns with a visible label and an error message.

```tsx
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"
import { Label } from "@/components/ui/label"

<div className="grid gap-2">
  <Label htmlFor="email">Email</Label>
  <Input id="email" type="email" aria-invalid={!!error} />
  {error ? <p className="text-sm text-destructive">{error}</p> : null}
</div>
```
